// One element written per call through an output parameter, «N» calls over
// «N» elements. `<~` works on the caller's variable, so a call costs what the
// write costs; an engine that copies in and writes back copies the collection
// on every call.
poner(t<~, i, v) { t[i]$~ v }
t = []
@ i:1..«N» { t$+ 0 }
@ k:1..«N» { poner(t<~, (k % «N») + 1, k) }
>> t[1] + t$# ¶
